* Super fast, no registration needed setup.\nL237:   * Get started watching and receiving website change notifications straight away.\nL238:   * See our cite125†tutorials and how-to page for more inspiration†changedetection.io L239: ## AI-powered website change detection — smart alerts and plain-language summaries\nL240: \nL241: Stop drowning in noise. Connect any LLM (OpenAI, Gemini, Anthropic, Ollama and more) and go from \"something changed\" to \"only the thing you care about changed\".\nL242: AI change detection rules — write a plain-English intent once: \"notify me only when the price drops below $50\", \"alert me when the item comes back in stock\", \"ignore navigation and footer changes\". The AI evaluates every detected diff against your intent and silently suppresses everything irrelevant. Fewer false positives, zero noise.\nL243: AI change summaries — instead of staring at a raw diff, your notification reads \"Price dropped from $89.99 to $67.00\" or \"3 new products added to the listing\". Works globally or per-watch, with full control over the prompt.\nL244: Works with any model you already pay for — GPT-4o-mini and Gemini Flash handle this well at fractions of a cent per check. Or run it entirely locally with Ollama, vLLM, LM Studio, or any OpenAI-compatible self-hosted endpoint — pick the OpenAI-compatible (vLLM, LM Studio, llama.cpp) option in the provider dropdown and point it at your server's `/v1` URL. Powered by cite126†LiteLLM , giving you seamless access to cite127†100+ supported providers and models†docs.litellm.ai .\nL245: Note: Available in our subscription/hosted service from June 2026\nL246: ### Target specific parts of the webpage using the Visual Selector tool.\nL247: \nL248: Available when connected to a cite128†playwright content fetcher (included as part of our subscription service)\nL249: \nL250: ### Easily see what changed, examine by word, line, or individual character.\nL251: ### Perform interactive browser steps\nL252: \nL253: Fill in text boxes, click buttons and more, setup your changedetection scenario.\nL254: \nL255: Using the Browser Steps configuration, add basic steps before performing change detection, such as logging into websites, adding a product to a cart, accept cookie logins, entering dates and refining searches.\nL256: \nL257: After Browser Steps have been run, then visit the Visual Selector tab to refine the content you're interested in. Requires Playwright to be enabled.\nL258: ### Awesome restock and price change notifications\nL259: \nL260: Enable the \"Re-stock & Price detection for single product pages\" option to activate the best way to monitor product pricing, this will extract any meta-data in the HTML page and give you many options to follow the pricing of the product.\nL261: \nL262: Easily organise and monitor prices for products from the dashboard, get alerts and notifications when the price of a product changes or comes back in stock again!\nL263: #### Monitor price change and restock trends over time as a graph, identify patterns, buy at the right time!\nL264: \nL265: Set price change notification parameters, upper and lower price, price change percentage and more. Always know when a product for sale drops in price.\nL266: ### Example use cases\nL267:   * Products and services have a change in pricing\nL268:   * Out of stock notification and Back In stock notification\nL269:   * Monitor and track PDF file changes, know when a PDF file has text changes.\nL270:   * Governmental department updates (changes are often only on their websites)\nL271:   * New software releases, security advisories when you're not on their mailing list.\nL272:   * Festivals with changes\nL273:   * Discogs restock alerts and monitoring\nL274:   * Realestate listing changes\nL275:   * Know when your favourite whiskey is on sale, or other special deals are announced before anyone else\nL276:   * COVID related news from government websites\nL277:   * University/organisation news from their website\nL278:   * Detect and monitor changes in JSON API responses\nL279:   * JSON API monitoring and alerting\nL280:   * Changes in legal and other documents\nL281:   * Trigger API calls via notifications when text appears on a website\nL282:   * Glue together APIs using the JSON filter and JSON notifications\nL483: ### Topics\nL484: \nL485: cite74†back-in-stock cite75†change-alert cite76†change-detection cite77†change-monitoring cite78†monitoring cite79†notifications cite80†restock-monitor cite81†rss cite82†self-hosted cite83†url-monitor cite84†web-scraping cite85†website-change-detection cite86†website-change-detector cite87†website-change-monitor cite88†website-change-notification cite89†website-change-tracker cite90†website-defacement-monitoring cite91†website-monitor cite92†website-monitoring cite93†website-watcher L486: \nL487: ### Resources\nL488: \nL489: cite94†Readme L490: \nL491: cite95†Apache-2.0 license L492: ### Contributing\nL493: \nL494: cite96†Contributing L495: \nL496: cite97†Activity L497: \nL498: ### Stars\nL499: \nL500: 35.0k stars\nL501: \nL502: ### Watchers\nL503: \nL504: 120 watching\nL505: \nL506: ### Forks\nL507: \nL508: cite98†2.1k forks L509: \nL510: cite99†Report repository L511: \nL512: ## Releases\nL513: \nL514: ## Packages\nL515: \nL516: ## Used by\nL517: \nL518: ## Contributors\nL519: \nL520: ## Languages\nL521: \nL522: You can’t perform that action at this time.\n"
